course: dictionary
lesson: 8400
title: Working out a sports word
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: You can work out a new word from the words around it. This is called context. «In rugby union a try, worth 5, needs the ball pressed down on or over the opponents' goal line.» You may not know what a try is, but the clues are worth 5 and ball pressed down. A try must be a way of scoring.
explain: Look for the clue words in «Rugby is a team game played with an oval ball» (the sentence in the dictionary). Team tells you more than one person plays. Oval ball tells you the ball is not round. Kick, carry and pass are things players do. Put these together and you know rugby is a sport.
explain: Some words come from places. Rugby got its name from Rugby School in England. When you meet a new word, ask yourself whether it might be named after a place, a person or a thing. Then check your guess in the sentence and in a dictionary.
fact: Rugby is a team game played with an oval ball.
fact: Players can kick the ball, carry it and pass it backwards.
fact: Players score by putting the ball down over the other team's line.
fact: «Try» means a score in rugby, worth 5 points in rugby union.
fact: Rugby is very popular in the UK, Ireland, Australia, New Zealand, South Africa and France.
exercise: What is rugby? | A swimming race | A type of cake | *A team game played with an oval ball | A kind of dance
exercise: In rugby, which way can a player pass the ball? | Upwards to the crowd | Forwards over the line only | *Backwards | Into the goal from the stands
exercise: «In rugby union a try, worth 5, needs the ball pressed down on or over the opponents' goal line.» Find and copy one word that is a way of scoring. | needs | ball | *try | opponents
test: How do players score in rugby? | By passing the ball forwards | *By putting the ball down over the other team's line | By kicking the ball into a basket | By running out of the pitch
test: Where did the name rugby come from? | The All Blacks team | A type of ball | A town in Scotland | *Rugby School in England
exam: Rugby is a game where two teams play with an oval ball, so it is best described as: | Dance | Individual | Water sport | *Team game
